#!ipxe
#
# Netboots Omarchy via the NBD bridge instead of archiso's stock
# archiso_pxe_http hook -- avoids the forced full-squashfs-to-RAM copy
# that hook always does. See ../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md for the full picture.
#
# iso_url points straight at Omarchy's own official host -- confirmed it
# serves the whole, unmodified ISO with proper Range support (Accept-Ranges,
# real 206/Content-Range replies), so there's no reason to re-host that
# ~6GB file ourselves. repo_base is real static hosting too (GitHub Pages,
# lagsoftware.com/files), and base (kernel/initrd) is now a GitHub Release
# -- see below. Nothing here depends on any machine of ours staying on.
#
# Whichever ISO version iso_url points at, base's vmlinuz/initrd MUST be
# extracted from that *exact same* build. Confirmed the hard way: a
# different build's kernel (module dir 6.19.13-arch1-1, generic) paired
# against this ISO's squashfs (7.1.8-arch1-...-t2, the T2 Mac kernel) boots
# fine up through a live shell, but fails partway through a real install
# (dm_mod/other modules for the running kernel don't exist in the squashfs
# at all). Re-extract and re-host base whenever iso_url's version changes.
#
# base's vmlinuz/initrd (~250MB combined -- over GitHub's 100MB hard
# per-file *push* limit, so these couldn't just join repo_base on lagsite
# the way the small files did) live as GitHub Release assets instead --
# confirmed Range support the same way as iso_url (real 206/Content-Range,
# backed by Azure Blob under the hood despite the github.com URL).
#
# Only two things get injected into the base initramfs, both from this
# repo:
#   - hook/archiso_pxe_nfs        (repurposed slot, starts the bridge)
#   - bridge/omarchy-nbd-bridge   (the compiled binary)
#
# archiso_nbd_srv=127.0.0.1 + archiso_nbd_name=archiso: archiso's STOCK,
# UNMODIFIED archiso_pxe_nbd hook (already present in Omarchy's initramfs,
# no injection needed for it) connects to our locally-running bridge as if
# it were any other NBD server. copytoram=n tells it not to copy anything
# to RAM -- confirmed against the actual archiso_pxe_nbd source that this
# is respected, not overridden the way the HTTP hook forces it.

set base https://github.com/logangeorge01/lagsite/releases/download/omarchy-4.0.0-boot/
set repo_base https://lagsoftware.com/files
set iso_url https://iso.omarchy.org/omarchy-4.0.0.iso

set ipparam BOOTIF=${netX/mac} ip=dhcp net.ifnames=0

# Clear any images already loaded in this iPXE session (from browsing the
# menu, or an earlier attempt) before loading ours -- netboot.xyz's own
# live-omarchy.ipxe does this for exactly this reason. Skipping it let
# leftover images get concatenated in alongside ours, corrupting the
# combined initrd blob: confirmed as the actual cause of the "VFS: Unable
# to mount root fs" panics -- it happened identically with netboot.xyz's
# own kernel+initrd (already proven working earlier in this project) once
# reached via a chain that skipped imgfree, not just with the T2 kernel.
imgfree

kernel ${base}vmlinuz ${ipparam} archisobasedir=arch archiso_nbd_srv=127.0.0.1 archiso_nbd_name=archiso copytoram=n archiso_nbd_bridge_url=${iso_url} module_blacklist=nvidia,nvidia_modeset,nvidia_uvm,nvidia_drm,pcspkr nouveau.modeset=1 i915.modeset=1 radeon.modeset=1 initrd=initrd.magic console=tty1 plymouth.enable=0 drm.panic_screen=kmsg systemd.log_level=debug ignore_loglevel
initrd ${base}initrd
initrd ${repo_base}/archiso_pxe_nfs /hooks/archiso_pxe_nfs mode=755
initrd ${repo_base}/omarchy-nbd-bridge /usr/local/bin/omarchy-nbd-bridge mode=755
boot
